Validate JSON instances against a JSON Schema

Usage: jsonschema-cli validate [OPTIONS] [SCHEMA]

Arguments:
  [SCHEMA]  The JSON Schema to validate with (e.g. schema.json). When omitted, each instance's own `$schema` property names the schema to validate it against

Options:
  -i, --instance <FILE>...         A path to a JSON instance (e.g. filename.json) to validate. May be specified multiple times or with multiple values after a single flag (e.g. `-i a.json b.json`)
  -d, --draft <DRAFT>              Enforce a specific JSON Schema draft [possible values: 4, 6, 7, 2019, 2020]
      --assert-format              Turn ON format validation
      --no-assert-format           Turn OFF format validation
      --vocabulary <URI>           Declare support for a vocabulary required by the meta-schema (may be repeated)
      --output <OUTPUT>            Output style [default: text] [possible values: text, flag, list, hierarchical]
      --errors-only                Only show validation errors
      --connect-timeout <SECONDS>  Timeout for establishing connections (in seconds)
      --timeout <SECONDS>          Total timeout for HTTP requests (in seconds)
  -k, --insecure                   Skip TLS certificate verification (dangerous!)
      --cacert <FILE>              Path to a custom CA certificate file (PEM format)
      --offline                    Refuse to fetch remote references
  -h, --help                       Print help
